      "quote_britannica": "OUNCE, a little weight, the fitteenth part of a pound avoirdupois, and the wealth part of a pound troy",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The ounce (/ ˈ aʊ n s /) is any of several different units of mass, weight, or volume and is derived almost unchanged from the uncia, an Ancient Roman unit of measurement"
